  "heading": "\\mean.value.theorem",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Mean Value Theorem}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\mean.value.theorem]\nTheorem:\ngiven:\n. a, b is \\real\n. f is \\function:on{\\reals..R}:to{\\reals..R}\nwhere:\n. a \\:real.less?:/ b\nthen:\n. exists: c is \\real\n  suchThat:\n  . a \\:real.less?:/ c\n  . c \\:real.less?:/ b\n  . f(b) \\.real.-./ f(a) = (\\derivative:of{f}:at{c}) \\.real.*./ (b \\.real.-./ a)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Mean Value Theorem\"\n. description: \"For differentiable $f$, there is a point $c \\in (a, b)$ where\n                the instantaneous rate of change equals the average rate of\n                change.\"\nId: \"31c0c6c3-b04e-48c3-b6b3-37990aa819cd\"",
